ation to the 2016 Census, and (ii) during the interview the Australian Statistician referred to legal advice received from the Australian Government Solicitor; and (b) there be laid on the table no later than 3 pm on Wednesday, 14 September 2016 by the Minister representing the Minister for Small Business, the legal advice referred to by the Australian Statistician during his appearance on 7.30 on 3 August 2016. James McGrath I seek leave to make a short statement. Stephen Parry Leave is granted for one minute. James McGrath The longstanding practice of successive governments has been not to disclose privileged legal advice. Stephen Parry The question is that the motion, as amended, moved by Senator Xenophon be agreed to.","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-senate-4282","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2016-09-12/1"}
